<%# The house's own note at the foot of a follow-up for a show it presented but
    did not produce. The visiting company's message leads the email; this is the
    landlord introducing itself afterwards, which is why it is boxed off as a
    callout rather than run in with the letter.

    Renamed from _tw_host_callout when the copy was genericized. %>
<table class="callout w410" width="410" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
  <tr>
    <th class="callout-inner secondary">
      <h5 align="left" class="article-title">
        <i>A note from <%= theater_info.name %></i>
      </h5>
      <% if local_assigns[:welcome_pitch] %>
      <div align="left" class="article-content">
        <p>
          <% personal = theater_info.first_person? %>
          <%= personal ? "I'd" : "We'd" %> like to take this opportunity to welcome you to <%= theater_info.name %>.
          There's a ton happening here, some of which is listed in the sidebar to the right,
          and <%= personal ? 'I hope' : 'we hope' %> you'll have a chance to check out some more.
        </p>
      </div>
      <% end %>
      <%= render 'house_pride', order: order %>
      <%= render 'tell_us_about_it', order: order %>
      <%= render 'stay_in_touch', order: order %>
    </th>
    <th class="expander"></th>
  </tr>
</table>
